{"answer": "No. Under the current design the chat client must not clear `busy` on an `error` frame. `busy` stays true from send until the run's terminator, and the only terminators are `stream_end` and socket close. Issue #191 changed this. Before it, task `044` cleared `busy` on `stream_end`, on an `error` frame, or on socket close. The engine change in #148 made `stream_end` the single terminal frame, sent once per accepted message. A probe had found an unrelated `INVALID_MESSAGE` error landing between two `entry_delta` frames of a healthy stream. A client that cleared `busy` on any `error` frame would drop the typing indicator and unlock the composer mid-answer. The spec (FR-013) requires a test that an `error` frame alone never clears `busy`. A `SERVER_ERROR` frame leaves the client busy until the following `stream_end`. The error frame still sets `state.error`. FR-014 also says a `RATE_LIMITED` error leaves `busy` unchanged.", "sources": ["issue-191 (re-cinq/Otto #191)", "specs/support-agent-chat/spec.md (FR-013, FR-014, Problem Statement)", "apps/web/test/useHalChat.test.tsx"]}
```

